WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.450
Your body cells each carry a full
set of chromosomes from your

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.670
mother, and a full
set from your father.

3
00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:10.690
A baby begins when a sperm
cell and an egg cell join.

4
00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:14.030
So shouldn't the baby end up with
twice as many chromosomes as

5
00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:14.510
its parents?

6
00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:17.890
And its own children
twice as many again?

7
00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.150
Why doesn't the number keep doubling?

8
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.670
In this mission, you'll meet meiosis,

9
00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:25.530
the cell division that
makes sperm and egg cells.

10
00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:28.830
You'll see how it makes four
cells that are all genetically

11
00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:29.990
different.

12
00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:32.130
And you'll compare it with mitosis,

13
00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:34.470
which makes identical copies.

14
00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:38.910
Your mission: explain why the
chromosome number never doubles.
